#
# Pre-create /lenovocust mount point before mount_all --early.
#
# Lenovo's vendor init.mt6897.rc:
#   on fs
#     mount_all --early       <- tries to mount /dev/block/by-name/lenovocust
#   on late-fs
#     mkdir /lenovocust       <- too late, mount already attempted
#
# Stock A16 ships its own init binary that auto-creates mount-point dirs
# inside fs_mgr before mounting. AOSP/LOS init does NOT, so mount_all --early
# silently fails for /lenovocust, the partition never mounts, and PQ services
# return bogus state because they can't load per-panel color tables from
# /lenovocust/disp_pq/. Without PQ, HWC drops every composition job as "no
# visible layer" and the boot animation never reaches the panel.
#
# Fix: mkdir the mount point in on early-fs (before any mount_all), so
# Lenovo's mount_all --early in on fs finds it. Permissions match Lenovo's
# late-fs mkdir (0777 system system).

on early-fs
    mkdir /lenovocust 0777 system system
